=== 2 genes flagged as alignment-limited ===
  OG0000120: 16 substitutions span only 31 codons of 217 (p=4.45e-14, Holm 3.56e-13)
  OG0000067: 4 substitutions span only 6 codons of 89 (p=3.46e-04, Holm 2.42e-03)

  These are not adaptive substitution lists. A dense run of changes
  in a few dozen codons is one localized event however many codons
  it spans, so each flagged gene contributes one uncertain event,
  not n independent ones. Do not name their residues as candidate
  adaptive sites.

  Do NOT draw a mechanism from the gap columns below:
    OG0000120: gaps at the substitution columns 0.0% against 14.5% for the gene.
    OG0000067: gaps at the substitution columns 0.0% against 12.4% for the gene.
    This is circular. Step 2 admits a site only when every codon
    position reconstructs at PP >= 0.90 and the ingroup is
    strictly monomorphic, which a column gapped in a third of
    the taxa cannot satisfy, so the filter selects gap-free
    columns and a low number here is guaranteed. It says nothing
    about whether the surrounding block is well aligned.
    Measure that over the block with a sliding window instead.

=== effect on the counts ===
  non-synonymous fixed differences, all genes : 60
  in flagged genes                           : 20 (33%)
  surviving                                  : 40 across 18 genes

  largest single contributor removed: OG0000120 with 16 changes
  Before this screen that one gene supplied 27% of the whole
  non-synonymous total, which is the dominance step 2 flagged.

=== what this does and does not change ===
  The MK test itself is NOT affected: alpha is estimated from counts
  over all sites, and removing sites post hoc because they cluster
  would bias it. This screen governs which individual loci and
  residues may be NAMED as candidates, which is a separate claim.
  Report both numbers and the screen, so a reviewer can see that the
  named candidates were filtered and the test statistic was not.

